From a06766cafbeacc4415a3666edca1dc0412a8d924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <jelon@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:37:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 006/206] port(3.12.2): simulator_arm64 -- A2/A5/B4/C1-C7 hooks

Done as a real 3-way merge (git merge-file --diff3, base 37bbc285d8d) rather
than a checkout, because both sides edit overlapping regions: we insert ~166
lines near InvokeFloatLeafRuntime while upstream inserts ~173 near
DoRedirectedCall, and both sides touch JumpToFrame.

Result: simulator_arm64.h merged with zero conflicts; .cc had only 2, both
macro-name collisions at the file's guard and trailer, resolved ours-wins.

Verified: upstream's work survives (DoRedirectedCall, ClobberVolatileRegisters,
DecodeAtomicMemory, SimulatorSetjmpBuffer all present) and so does ours
(SetPendingVmcodeFile, s_base_instructions_ptr_, fhp_shorebird_load_vmcode,
ShorebirdSimToCpu, IsHostCodeAddress). Diffing our added lines against the 3.7
original leaves only the macro rename. #if/#endif nesting balances to 0.

The inner guard on the B4 C shims is renamed, not retargeted to
SIMULATOR_AVAILABLE -- under FHP_NO_SIMULATOR_CODEGEN they compile out. That is
the pre-existing semantics; changing it is a design decision, not a port.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

